  `Submonoid.powers_eq_closure`,
  `regularLocalRing_uniqueFactorizationMonoid`,
  `IsLocalization.isDomain_of_le_nonZeroDivisors`;
- best owner abstraction: the canonical Picard owner is still `CommRing.Pic`, but the relevant
  upstream bridge for the nontrivial localization branch is the Chapter 10 Nagata owner for
  factoriality of localizations at multiplicative subsets generated by
  `Submonoid.closure {p | Prime p}`; the local-ring Picard owner applies only in the
  unit-localization branch;
- primitive vs. derived:
  the primitive data is the regular-local structure on `R` and the chosen element `f`; the
  source-facing theorem remains about `Localization.Away f`, while the factoriality of the
  nonunit branch and the Picard triviality of the unit branch are both derived from upstream owner
  abstractions rather than from any local wrapper API;
- source/core/bridge triage:
  `source-facing`: the theorem below for `Localization.Away f`;
  `core/canonical`: the upstream `Subsingleton (CommRing.Pic S)` owner;
